  "academyNote": "As per the Governance handbook, academies and free schools can choose to set their own term dates.",
  "localFacts": [
    {
      "fact": "In 2027-28 Gloucestershire does not tie the spring break to Easter: term 4 runs to 7 April 2028 and term 5 starts on Monday 24 April, so the break (10 to 21 April) includes Good Friday and Easter Monday.",
      "source": "https://www.gloucestershire.gov.uk/media/cu0ktbnh/gloucestershire-school-term-dates-and-holidays-for-academic-year-2027-28.pdf"
    },
    {
      "fact": "Schools may hold up to five INSET days within term time, so the first or last day of term for pupils can differ from school to school.",
      "source": "https://www.gloucestershire.gov.uk/education-and-learning/term-dates/"
    },
    {
      "fact": "The council publishes six terms and the number of days in each: 39, 35, 30, 24, 34 and 33 in 2026-27, a total of 195.",
      "source": "https://www.gloucestershire.gov.uk/education-and-learning/term-dates/"
    },
    {
      "fact": "Schools considering other dates or changes to opening times are advised to contact the council's Transport Team and local childcare providers about the impact.",
      "source": "https://www.gloucestershire.gov.uk/media/cu0ktbnh/gloucestershire-school-term-dates-and-holidays-for-academic-year-2027-28.pdf"
    },
    {
      "fact": "Schools may decide individually or collectively which five days in the year are INSET or non-contact days.",
      "source": "https://www.gloucestershire.gov.uk/media/cu0ktbnh/gloucestershire-school-term-dates-and-holidays-for-academic-year-2027-28.pdf"
    },
    {
      "fact": "The 2026-27 year starts on Tuesday 1 September 2026 and ends on Wednesday 21 July 2027.",
      "source": "https://www.gloucestershire.gov.uk/education-and-learning/term-dates/"
    }
  ],
